{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha","id":1547325,"title":"PC Raksha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-30T02:52:51-08:00","id":1547325,"title":"PC Raksha","content":"I've always loved the raksha, are there still p!and to make pc rules for them? I know the original devs wanted to make a book for them, but the first time I read about them it was early 2012, almost 13 years ago now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T05:26:58-08:00","id":1547417,"title":"","content":"Personally, I haven't seen anything. I've had a version in mind myself for a while but I've found the Mountain Folk and Dragon Kings more compelling (and haven't really had the time to work on those either).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T11:42:33-08:00","id":1547428,"title":"","content":"They've pitched a book on the Wyld, including Fair Folk, but that was a few years back.<br /> <br /> They're not inclined to do playable raksha; Vance has said that the problem is there's no way they could do a single charmset for them that doesn't narrow the scope of their capabilities and standardise their power set, and some of the best stuff they've done for raksha is weird, idiosyncratic stuff that couldn't work with a charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T20:50:57-08:00","id":1547441,"title":"","content":"Any word on modeling them as really weird exigents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T00:18:56-08:00","id":1547478,"title":"","content":"The current edition has gotten rid of some of my favorite PC options. I think I'm probably going to try to convince my group to go back to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T00:59:16-08:00","id":1547481,"title":"","content":"Raksha were kind of a terrible option in 2e also. They were either playing their won game, or with the errata, a nightmare to book keep and still generally weaker than any Exalted option.<br /> <br /> Currently there are hopes to do Dragon Kings if we ever get <i>Towers of the Mighty</i>, and no where has shown-up to do Jadeborn but they are something hte current devs seem keen on doing as well when they can. Fair Folk just happen to as noted, be ill-suited for PCs in general.<br /> <br /> (My own take is that since 1e, I don't think Fair Folk should have been playable and that they would have been better served with abook like <i>Games of Divinity</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T01:52:02-08:00","id":1547482,"title":"","content":"Core raksha weren't very good, but post errata raksha were fun. I also loved playing fae blooded, I know they weren't very powerful compared to exalts but two of my favorite characters were fae blooded. Also sense mountain folk were an offshoot race of the raksha I don't see how you can have one without the other.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T02:30:24-08:00","id":1547483,"title":"","content":"Mountain Folk are a unified like, thing, in a way that raksha nobles aren't. Them being Fair Folk at this point has been pretty much vestigial since the 1e book, to a point their history as fae is almost a factoid like how the closest relatives to chrodates like us and fish are echynoderms like starfish.<br /> <br /> Kind of notably too, they were not in the book with the Fair Folk in 2e. They were with Dragon Kings, the for-sure other non-human species showcased in that edition and which have been, as I noted, proposed in a book this edition as well and will be playable in Essence.<br /> <br /> Additionally, a thing of note is that in 3e, not all fae creatures are raksha. Raksha specifically are nobles, and the various minor kinds of fae such as hobgoblins are different sorts of Wyld creature often subservient to them. So the Mountain Folk could be even more distantly related by that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T02:52:14-08:00","id":1547484,"title":"","content":"At that point just call them dwarves, that's all you have left. You will have ripped everything that makes the mountain folk different than generic dwarves out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T07:08:42-08:00","id":1547488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547441#post1547441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any word on modeling them as really weird exigents?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the biggest problem I've observed with adapting playable Fair Folk is that the their traits going to 7 instead of possessing dice adders doesn't play very well with static defence values. It's fine for an antagonist but for a player character? it's <i>boring</i> because it screens out a lot of potentially interesting weaker opponents because they can't realistically hit them (this wasn't obvious in 2e because there were bigger issues at play).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately that's been their most consistent trait since the first edition core and I think they'd lose a lot of their feel if one were to remove that in place of excellencies or dice tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T11:29:23-08:00","id":1547493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547488#post1547488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the biggest problem I've observed with adapting playable Fair Folk is that the their traits going to 7 instead of possessing dice adders doesn't play very well with static defence values. It's fine for an antagonist but for a player character? it's <i>boring</i> because it screens out a lot of potentially interesting weaker opponents because they can't realistically hit them (this wasn't obvious in 2e because there were bigger issues at play).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately that's been their most consistent trait since the first edition core and I think they'd lose a lot of their feel if one were to remove that in place of excellencies or dice tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, reminded of that, it doesn't seem like a workable idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T15:09:36-08:00","id":1547500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547484#post1547484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At that point just call them dwarves, that's all you have left. You will have ripped everything that makes the mountain folk different than generic dwarves out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stuff about Jadeborn being people carved form the earth by Autocthhon dealing with a diminished state and caste-based society fighting horrors locked below the surface of the world since the Time Before, and waiting for their deity to return, while utilizing a bunch of magitech power armor and equipment to do so has nothing to do with being Fair Folk-originally. Again, it's been vestigial since their first detailed appearance. Even the thing that would actually maybe link them to the fae, Chaso Pattern, never even gets a hint of that in either 1e or 2e.<br /> <br /> And save probably a different context of the Geas, Eternal War, and Castes as well as a bit more rock-person appearance, none of that seems to be on the docket to change this edition. What exactly is generic dwarf about not having something that is literally ancient pre-history that can't be confirmed or denied, and amounts to describing why they're jade egg souls. It's a hint on origin, but not anything that really matters for them being them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T06:48:16-08:00","id":1547514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547482#post1547482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Core raksha weren't very good, but post errata raksha were fun. I also loved playing fae blooded, I know they weren't very powerful compared to exalts but two of my favorite characters were fae blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should mention that god-blooded have been playable in Ex3 since Heirs to the Shogunate, it's a 5 dot merit that allows your PC to learn ancestry appropriate spirit charms that have the Eclipse keyword.<br /> <br /> Though I should note that this framework is primarily for god-blooded exalts who only need a few thematic abilities rather than basic &quot;quality of life&quot; stuff like having a mote pool, dice adders, ox-bodies etc so you'd need to figure those out if you wanted to have an unexalted god-blooded who can operate at terrestrial level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T17:33:21-08:00","id":1547525,"title":"","content":"Also the more open options for sorcerous initiation, one of the shaping rituals for Scarred By Nightmares has the sorcerer feeding on emotional energies like one of the Fair Folk and the merit Child of Madness gives you wyld immunity in exchange for an iron vulnerability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T17:51:23-08:00","id":1547526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547482#post1547482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also sense mountain folk were an offshoot race of the raksha I don't see how you can have one without the other.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Their powers and other rules weren't particularly similar even when they were packaged together in the same book.<br /> <br /> Unless Mountain Folk were being radically rewritten, there would be a uniformity to them that would be conductive to providing a common Charm set in a way that might not work when the new writing wants to emphasize the grand diversity of the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Like, God help writers for prior Editions they really tried their best to make a Charm set that felt as though you could construct a wide variety of strange and wondrous dark angel nobility out of, but it always ran into boundaries that illustrated the lie of that, how the only way it could work was by making their diversity only function at the surface level. No, I think it's probably better to go with them along similar lines to spirits; almost entirely NPCs provided with custom powers evocative of the specific character, who can come in any number of forms and functions even if there are some common principles.<br /> <br /> A person might talk about their memorable playable fae-blooded, but... what was being used to model them? A range of access to Charms virtually indistinguishable to raksha, but where they were also made out of flesh and blood?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T07:22:28-08:00","id":1547543,"title":"","content":"Anyway, if people want playable Fair Folk homebrew <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/930959-3e-raksha-homebrew\">this</a> was one of the most comprehensive attempts I've seen.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T15:51:12-08:00","id":1547560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547500#post1547500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The stuff about Jadeborn being people carved form the earth by Autocthhon dealing with a diminished state and caste-based society fighting horrors locked below the surface of the world since the Time Before, and waiting for their deity to return, while utilizing a bunch of magitech power armor and equipment to do so has nothing to do with being Fair Folk-originally. Again, it's been vestigial since their first detailed appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>So very much this. The connection to the Raksha was <i>dropped into borderline irrelevance</i> and little more than a footnote of the Mountain <i>the moment they are introduced to us as the Jadeborn</i>, back in E:FF from 1e. <b><i>Everything </i></b>that has come to define the Jadeborn as we know is <i>based on their complete divergence</i> of the Raksha in almost all aspects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547500#post1547500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the thing that would actually maybe link them to the fae, Chaso Pattern, never even gets a hint of that in either 1e or 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, considering that &quot;Chaos Pattern&quot;has always been very much of a misnomer, coming not from any hints or signs whatsoever of ressonance with dreams or the wyld but from the socially disruptive effects - what in itself tells us of how far the Jadeborn have gone from grasping what true chaos can mean - its wielders can have due to how the intersection of being able to see and interact with the strands of Fate plays haywire with the Geas and their own mindset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547500#post1547500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And save probably a different context of the Geas, Eternal War, and Castes as well as a bit more rock-person appearance, none of that seems to be on the docket to change this edition. What exactly is generic dwarf about not having something that is literally ancient pre-history that can't be confirmed or denied, and amounts to describing why they're jade egg souls. It's a hint on origin, but not anything that really matters for them being them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, even the 1e PG indirectly admitted through god-blooded character creation rules that in many ways the Mountain Folk have more in common with earth elementals than fae proper.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T02:39:53-08:00","id":1547571,"title":"","content":"I always thought this was the intended origin of the Chaos Pattern but the fact I have to go all the way back to 1st edition to find this lore suggests it's maybe not that important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted: the Fair Folk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autochthon moved through the world long after most of his brethren withdrew to Heaven. In his wake, he trailed wonders and miracles such as the wisest craftsmen of the First Age could only vainly emulate. His will awakened stone and metal to dimly reflect his power, as he enchanted jade, orichalcum, moonsilver and nameless ores depleted from the world and memory. As he completed one project, the Primordial sought the materials for another, and in this fashion, he stumbled upon the sleeping Fair Folk, bound in jade. As he had done before innumerable times and would innumerably again, Autochthon set the jade before him and brought the force of his power to bear to shape and transmute the stone. The fae within stirred, and though its will dwarfed in comparison to the Primordial\u2019s, the resistance of a sentient presence marred the design. Rather than incensed, Autochthon grew intrigued and beheld the chaos within the rock and the pattern of power he imposed upon it. <b>He discarded the sphere and withdrew another nodule</b>, and this one also bore the spark of unformed possibility. He breathed upon the second stone and shaped it more lightly, as the other Primordials had shaped the gods and laid their touch upon the Dragon Kings. Guided by the half-formed designs that would ultimately become humanity, Autochthon assembled the first of the Mountain Folk in the rough-hewn shape of man. The creature did not remember other than it was, not of the Wyld or the torpid Ages locked within stone. Its life began with the will of the Great Maker.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-07T20:49:50-08:00","id":1547627,"title":"","content":"I think most of the lore around Chaos Pattern attributes it to the Pattern Spiders also having been created by Autocthon, and by extension some nascent connection to the Loom (hence the TN reducers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-08T05:44:24-08:00","id":1547631,"title":"","content":"For my games I created The One Before The First who <i>isn't necessarily real</i> but an idea in Mountain Folk culture that the being the discarded sphere eventually became has bedevilled them from the shadows and tempts them away from perfect harmony that it can never partake in. Artisans are divided on if this is some boogie man the lower castes invented or thinking it makes perfect sense that Chaos Pattern originated from a being that was similar to The First.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-09T12:34:41-08:00","id":1547649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1547325-pc-raksha?p=1547627#post1547627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most of the lore around Chaos Pattern attributes it to the Pattern Spiders also having been created by Autocthon, and by extension some nascent connection to the Loom (hence the TN reducers).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit what I mean where the place you'd <i>think</i> they would have linked them to their Wyld origins...they aren't. It's just more Autochthon things. Again, they're as much Fair Folk as we're mushrooms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}